insert into documents (doc_type,title,source_url,doc_date,body) values ('news','Storm Impacts & Operations Updates - July 3, 2026 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/storm-impacts-operations-updates-july-3-2026/','2026-07-03','Storm Impacts & Operations Updates - July 3, 2026 - Jul 03, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices As cleanup efforts continue across Ramara, Township crews remain focused on restoring normal conditions following this week''s storm. We would like to thank residents for their patience, cooperation and the many neighbours who have been checking in on one another. Cooling & Hydration Stations Open To support residents affected by ongoing power outages and the current extreme heat, the Township has again opened the following facilities today as cooling areas: • Township Administration Building (2297 Highway 12, Brechin) – open until 4:30 p.m. • Ramara Centre (5482 Highway 12, Atherley) – open until 6 p.m. Residents are welcome to visit these locations during operating hours to cool down, recharge and take refuge from the heat. Roads & Cleanup • Concession Road 2 has reopened. • Lakeshore Drive remains closed between Simcoe Road and Concession Road 2 due to ongoing work in the area. • A tree remains down at Concession Road 8 and Sideroad 15, and work in the area is ongoing. Please continue to use caution when travelling, as crews remain active throughout Ramara. Some roads may still have tree debris along ditches and shoulders. These areas will continue to be cleaned up next week following the completion of priority roadway work. Parks Update Township crews will begin assessing and cleaning up parks next week, following the completion of priority roadway cleanup. Parks and waterfront areas along Lake Simcoe, from Atherley to the Talbot River, including municipally owned waterfront parks, may have storm-related debris or damage. Residents are encouraged to use caution when visiting these areas. Generator Safety With ongoing power outages, please continue to use generators safely: • Never operate a generator inside your home, garage, shed or any enclosed space. • Keep generators outdoors and well away from windows, doors and vents. • Ensure your home has working carbon monoxide (CO) alarms. • If your CO alarm sounds, or anyone experiences symptoms such as headache, dizziness or nausea, move to fresh air immediately and call 911. Ramara Fire & Rescue Services continues to respond to generator-related calls following the storm. Please use generators safely to protect yourself and your family. Power Line Safety Stay at least 10 metres away from any downed power line. Always assume a fallen power line is energized and dangerous. Report downed power lines to Hydro One at 1-800-434-1235. Report Township Hazards To report hazardous road conditions, fallen trees or other Township infrastructure concerns, please call the Township at 705-484-5374 (option 9 after-hours). Thank you for your continued patience and cooperation as crews continue storm cleanup. Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Storm Impacts & Operations Updates - July 3, 2026 (7 p.m.) | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/storm-impacts-operations-updates-july-3-2026-7-pm/','2026-07-03','Storm Impacts & Operations Updates - July 3, 2026 (7 p.m.) - Jul 03, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices Road Closure Update Please note that Lakeshore Drive and Sideroad 15 have reopened. While roads have reopened, some impacted areas still have branches and debris along roadsides. Please drive with caution and watch for crews working throughout the Township. Township crews will continue storm cleanup and debris removal throughout next week. Tree & Brush Disposal Residents can dispose of storm-related brush and tree debris by taking materials to a County waste facility (fees may apply) or through the County of Simcoe''s regular yard waste collection program. The next yard waste collection in Ramara is scheduled for the week of July 6. Please have materials at the curb by 7 a.m. on Monday, and crews will collect them at some point during the week. The following collection is scheduled for the week of July 20. For yard waste preparation guidelines, visit: https://simcoe.ca/.../org.../special-collections/yard-waste/. Power Line Safety Stay at least 10 metres away from any downed power line. Always assume a fallen power line is energized and dangerous. Report downed power lines to Hydro One at 1-800-434-1235. Report Township Hazards To report hazardous road conditions, fallen trees or other Township infrastructure concerns, please call the Township at 705-484-5374 - Option 9. Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Lagoon City Canal Maintenance Update – July 21, 2026 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/lagoon-city-canal-maintenance-update-july-21-2026/','2026-07-21','Lagoon City Canal Maintenance Update – July 21, 2026 - Jul 21, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices The Township of Ramara is pleased to advise residents that authorization from the Federal Department of Fisheries and Oceans (DFO) has been received to proceed with skimming and mechanical aquatic weed harvesting activities within Lagoon City''s canal system. Township crews are mobilizing immediately, and canal weed harvesting operations will begin today (July 21, 2026). Residents are encouraged to visit ramara.ca/canals for the latest harvesting routes and updates. We sincerely appreciate the patience and understanding of residents throughout this process and recognize the significant impacts the current condition of the canals has had on navigation, recreation and residents'' enjoyment of the waterways. The Township of Ramara owns and operates Lagoon City''s canal system. With that ownership comes the responsibility to ensure maintenance activities are carried out safely, responsibly and in compliance with applicable legislation and regulatory requirements. We remain committed to maintaining Lagoon City''s canals and lagoons while balancing navigability, environmental stewardship, and the protection of fish habitat and the broader aquatic ecosystem. As part of the 2027 Budget process, staff will bring forward recommendations to Council and the Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission for an operational study to evaluate maintenance strategies, technologies and performance measures to support the future management of the canal system. We recognize that residents have seen changes to the Canal Maintenance Program over the past two years. As legislative requirements, regulatory expectations and industry best practices continue to evolve, the Township has a responsibility to adapt its practices to ensure the program is delivered safely, responsibly and in compliance with applicable legislation. The Township also recognizes there has been considerable discussion and many questions regarding this year''s Canal Maintenance Program. To help provide additional context, residents are encouraged to review the Lagoon City Canal Maintenance Program Fact Sheet . Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Disaster Recovery Assistance for Ontarians (DRAO) Program Activated for April 2026 Flooding – Lake St. John Area, Ramara | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/disaster-recovery-assistance-for-ontarians-drao-program-activated-for-april-2026-flooding-lake-st-john-area-ramara/','2026-07-15','Disaster Recovery Assistance for Ontarians (DRAO) Program Activated for April 2026 Flooding – Lake St. John Area, Ramara - Jul 20, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices The Province of Ontario has announced that the Lake St. John area within the Township of Ramara has been designated as an activation area under the Disaster Recovery Assistance for Ontarians (DRAO) program for flooding that occurred in April 2026. Residents and property owners are encouraged to review the DRAO website , including the official activation area map , to determine whether their property is located within the designated activation area. Eligibility for the program is determined by the Province of Ontario. The purpose of the DRAO program is to return essential property to a basic level, make homes safe and habitable, and allow people to resume their livelihoods. The program is not intended to replace insurance and does not cover all costs. The program is administered by the Province of Ontario, which determines applicant eligibility and all funding decisions. Eligible private property owners may apply for assistance if they reside within the activation area, sustained damage as a result of flooding from lakes, rivers and creeks, and do not have insurance coverage for the damage or have insurance that is insufficient to cover eligible essential recovery costs. Damage to secondary residences such as a cottage or other recreational property is ineligible. Damage from sewer backup is also not generally eligible under the program. Sewer backup is water that comes up through floor drains or other connections to the sewer system. Insurance for sewer backup is widely available for purchase as part of homeowners’ insurance policies. An exception is made for low-income households as defined by the guidelines. For information about low-income household guidelines, view additional help for low-income families . In addition, damage to basements and crawl spaces is eligible to the extent required to return these areas to a safe, basic state. For example, financial assistance can be provided for clean-up, restoration of insulation/vapour barrier, and replacement of essentials like furnaces and hot water heaters. The costs to restore basement finishes (drywall, flooring, etc.) and furnishings are not eligible. The deadline to apply for the program is November 16, 2026. Guidelines and application forms are available on the DRAO website . Those affected by flooding are encouraged to contact their insurance provider to determine whether their damage is covered by insurance, prior to applying for the DRAO program. Any questions about the DRAO program can be sent to the Ministry of Municipal Affairs and Housing at: DisasterAssistance@Ontario.ca . Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Fire Hydrant Flow Testing Continues July 28 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/fire-hydrant-flow-testing-continues-july-28/','2026-08-10','Fire Hydrant Flow Testing Continues July 28 - Jul 13, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices Please be advised that the Ontario Clean Water Agency will be conducting fire hydrant flow testing in Brechin and Lagoon City. This critical testing ensures our municipal water supply and hydrant network can provide adequate pressure and flow in the event of an emergency. Testing Schedule Dates: July 14-15, July 21-22, July 28-29 Time: 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. Affected Areas : Municipal water users in Brechin and Lagoon City What to Expect During flow testing, increased water flow can temporarily stir up mineral sediment in the water main, causing water to appear yellow, brown or cloudy. The water remains safe for consumption. If discoloured water is detected, run the cold water tap closest to the water source for a few minutes, or until the water runs clear. If your water does not clear after flushing, or if you have any questions, please contact the Infrastructure Department at 705-484-5374 ext. 285. Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Touchdown! Youth Flag Football returns after a winning season | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/touchdown-youth-flag-football-returns-after-a-winning-season/','2026-08-10','Touchdown! Youth Flag Football returns after a winning season By Township of Ramara - Jul 14, 2026 Media Releases Register now to join Ramara''s popular youth flag football program this fall Ramara, Ont. / July 14, 2026 – Following an overwhelmingly successful season this spring, the Township of Ramara is proud to once again partner with SportsKlub to bring the Youth Flag Football program to the community this fall. "Seeing nearly 100 young athletes take part in our first season with this new partnership was an incredible success," said Mayor Basil Clarke. "The enthusiasm from participants, families, volunteers and our partners exceeded expectations, and we''re excited to build on that momentum this fall. Programs like this strengthen our community while encouraging healthy, active lifestyles for our youth." Building on the success of the spring season, the fall program will introduce a new age division, expanding opportunities for more youth to get involved. Participants can register in one of three age groups: 8 to 11 years, 12 to 14 years or 15 to 17 years. Registration is open for youth from Ramara, Orillia, and surrounding communities. The six-week program costs $60 to register and will run Tuesdays, Sept. 1 to Oct. 6, from 5 to 7 p.m. at the Ramara Centre fields. Should a session be cancelled due to inclement weather, games will be held the next day (Wednesday). Each participant will receive a team jersey, enjoy weekly photos and season highlights, and celebrate the end of the season with a pizza party generously sponsored by Tops In Pizza. "After an incredible first season, we''re thrilled to return to Ramara this fall," said Tyler Evans, Founder of SportsKlub. "The energy from the players and families was amazing, and we''re excited to welcome returning athletes while introducing even more youth to the game." To ensure enough time to prepare teams, order jerseys, and organize the season, registration is now open. Families are encouraged to register early, as space is limited and spots are expected to fill quickly. Register online at www.ramara.ca/recreation or contact the Ramara Recreation team at 705-325-3091. The Township of Ramara is grateful to SportsKlub for its continued partnership, as well as the dedicated coaches, volunteers and community supporters whose commitment helped make the inaugural season such a success. For more information about recreation programs, visit www.ramara.ca/recreation . -30- Media Contact Melissa Gowanlock Manager of Communications & Community Experience 705-484-5374 ext. 322 mgowanlock@ramara.ca Athletes take part in the Township of Ramara''s Youth Flag Football program. Registration is now underway for the fall season in partnership with SportsKlub. Families can register online at www.ramara.ca/recreation. Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!') on conflict (source_url) do nothing;